# Pasabayan Android — spec and iOS reference

## IDE workflow (authoritative)

- **Cursor:** editing and AI-assisted coding only. Do not assume Cursor’s embedded Java / Red Hat Java extension is the Gradle JDK.
- **Android Studio:** **Sync**, **Run**, **Gradle**, **JDK**, **emulator / device**, and **Build** are done here. Treat Android Studio as source of truth when Gradle fails in a terminal that inherited a bad `JAVA_HOME`, or when diagnosing `jlink` / `androidJdkImage` issues — fix via **Settings → Build, Execution, Deployment → Build Tools → Gradle → Gradle JDK** (use the **embedded JBR** or **JDK 17**).

If the user reports build problems, prefer Android Studio sync/logs over Cursor-only Java tooling.

